WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.720 --> 00:00:05.200
"Mortal Kombat Legends: Battle of the Realms"&nbsp;
follows the franchise's animated debut,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.200 --> 00:00:08.720
"Mortal Kombat Legends: Scorpion's&nbsp;
Revenge," which introduced viewers&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:08.720 --> 00:00:11.520
to an animated take on the Mortal Kombat universe.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:11.520 --> 00:00:16.000
Here's the ending of "Mortal Kombat&nbsp;
Legends: Battle of the Realms" explained.

00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:19.920
To begin discussing "Battle of the Realms,"&nbsp;
it's important to understand where "Scorpion's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:19.920 --> 00:00:24.880
Revenge" left off in the world of Mortal Kombat&nbsp;
Legends. As usual in most retellings of the famous&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:24.880 --> 00:00:29.680
original Mortal Kombat Tournament, Lord Raiden,&nbsp;
protector of Earthrealm and god of Thunder,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:29.680 --> 00:00:34.240
brings together Earth's champions to compete in&nbsp;
the Mortal Kombat tournament — designed by the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:34.240 --> 00:00:39.520
elder gods to allow the realms a chance to fight&nbsp;
for power over one another. In Earthrealm's case,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:39.520 --> 00:00:43.200
it's a chance to protect Earth from an&nbsp;
incursion by the forces of Outworld.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:43.200 --> 00:00:47.440
In the final moments of the tournament,&nbsp;
Scorpion intervenes and beheads Goro&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:47.440 --> 00:00:51.440
just before the monster can deliver a&nbsp;
finishing blow to Liu Kang. Scorpion&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:51.440 --> 00:00:56.880
also manages to trick Shang Tsung and obtains a&nbsp;
special key to free the mad elder god Shinnok.

00:00:56.880 --> 00:01:01.680
Thanks to Scorpion's interference, Earthrealm&nbsp;
wins the tournament and Liu Kang is crowned the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:01.680 --> 00:01:06.240
winner as a result. Scorpion kills Sub-Zero,&nbsp;
believing him to be the culprit behind the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:06.240 --> 00:01:11.200
orchestrated deaths of his family and clan, but&nbsp;
it's revealed that the Netherrealm sorcerer Quan&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:11.200 --> 00:01:16.160
Chi actually committed this heinous crime.&nbsp;
Scorpion finally obtains his revenge as he&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:16.160 --> 00:01:20.640
brutalizes the sorcerer before finishing&nbsp;
him off. In the aftermath of that fight,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:20.640 --> 00:01:24.480
Scorpion resigns himself to another&nbsp;
death as the island crumbles around him.

00:01:25.280 --> 00:01:29.360
After a short prologue, "Battle of the Realms"&nbsp;
quite literally begins with a battle between&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:29.360 --> 00:01:34.320
realms. Sometime after the tournament, Outworld&nbsp;
plans and enacts an invasion of Earthrealm.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:34.320 --> 00:01:38.880
Kitana, who is still under the thumb of Shao&nbsp;
Kahn, is leading the forces of Outworld in an&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:38.880 --> 00:01:44.960
all-out offensive. Special forces figures like&nbsp;
Sonya Blade, Jax Briggs, and Curtis Stryker take&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:44.960 --> 00:01:50.240
up defensive positions against the incursion with&nbsp;
the help of Kung Lao and Lord Raiden. Apparently,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:50.240 --> 00:01:54.480
Earthrealm's victory in the Mortal Kombat&nbsp;
tournament is being ignored by Shao Kahn.

00:01:54.480 --> 00:01:58.080
During the battle, Shao Kahn enters&nbsp;
the battlefield, but not to fight.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:58.080 --> 00:02:02.000
He offers Raiden a chance to resolve the&nbsp;
conflict through one final tournament,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:02.000 --> 00:02:07.440
and Raiden agrees, seizing the opportunity to&nbsp;
save future generations from the responsibility&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:07.440 --> 00:02:12.240
of defending Earthrealm by ending it all here&nbsp;
and now. Shao Kahn and Lord Raiden petition&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:12.240 --> 00:02:17.600
the elder gods to make the tournament happen.&nbsp;
Shockingly, Raiden also sacrifices his godhood&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:17.600 --> 00:02:22.320
in order to participate in the&nbsp;
tournament alongside his heroes.

00:02:22.320 --> 00:02:26.560
While the rest of the characters are waging&nbsp;
war against one another, Scorpion finds himself&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:26.560 --> 00:02:31.360
back in Netherrealm following his fated battle&nbsp;
with the villainous Quan Chi. However, instead&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:31.360 --> 00:02:36.400
of Quan Chi this time, it's Shinnok, a corrupt&nbsp;
elder god, who greets him. Waiting patiently,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:36.400 --> 00:02:41.520
Shinnok seeks to use the key Scorpion obtained&nbsp;
from Shang Tsung to unlock an ancient power. The&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:41.520 --> 00:02:46.400
problem is that the key has now fused itself with&nbsp;
Scorpion's soul, so Shinnok threatens Scorpion&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:46.400 --> 00:02:51.200
with eternal pain and torment should he not use&nbsp;
the power of the key on the Temple of Elements.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:51.200 --> 00:02:56.640
But Scorpion doesn't take kindly to threats, and&nbsp;
he quickly ditches the elder god and his minions.

00:02:56.640 --> 00:03:01.840
Elsewhere, Kuai Liang and Smoke, members of the&nbsp;
Lin Kuei, train before being commanded by their&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:01.840 --> 00:03:07.600
grandmaster to bring Scorpion in alive. Liang&nbsp;
is reluctant to accept the mantle of Sub-Zero,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:07.600 --> 00:03:12.320
but is emboldened by the thought of killing&nbsp;
Scorpion, who murdered his brother Bi-Han.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:12.320 --> 00:03:17.520
Ultimately, the grandmaster betrays his own clan&nbsp;
by damning them to a life of programmed servitude&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:17.520 --> 00:03:22.720
as cyborgs, and Cyrax and Sektor appear&nbsp;
as newly constructed cybernetic warriors.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:22.720 --> 00:03:27.920
The grandmaster wishes the same for Sub-Zero&nbsp;
and Smoke, and in their struggle to escape Cyrax&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:27.920 --> 00:03:32.640
and Sektor, Smoke is taken by the cyborgs&nbsp;
and eventually converted into one himself.

00:03:33.440 --> 00:03:38.400
As promised by Outworld's ruler Shao Kahn, as&nbsp;
well as Lord Raiden, a tournament commences that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:38.400 --> 00:03:43.040
tests the mettle of each realm's champions. True&nbsp;
to the video game franchise, the fights pack a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:43.040 --> 00:03:48.560
bone-crunching punch followed by countless buckets&nbsp;
of blood and gore. Some combatants lose, but are&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:48.560 --> 00:03:54.240
lucky enough to be spared a grisly death, like&nbsp;
Johnny Cage and Jax. Others aren't so fortunate.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:54.240 --> 00:03:58.960
Quickly, Curtis Stryker and Kung Lao are&nbsp;
eviscerated by prominent Outworld combatants&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:58.960 --> 00:04:05.040
Shang Tsung and Shao Kahn. The combat is bloody,&nbsp;
vicious, and thrilling for fans of the franchise.

00:04:05.040 --> 00:04:09.280
At a pivotal moment, Kitana is ordered&nbsp;
by Shao Kahn to fight Raiden, and while&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:09.280 --> 00:04:13.840
both are competent fighters, Kitana gains the&nbsp;
upper hand. Ready to unleash a killing blow,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:13.840 --> 00:04:18.960
Kitana strikes — seemingly hitting her true&nbsp;
target, Shao Kahn, with her blade. Seeking freedom&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:18.960 --> 00:04:23.840
from his tyranny for herself and the realms,&nbsp;
she defects and joins those opposing Outworld.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:23.840 --> 00:04:28.960
Shao Kahn, however, isn't finished; he vows to&nbsp;
make Kitana watch as he destroys the realms.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:28.960 --> 00:04:34.000
The tournament continues with Liu Kang and Shang&nbsp;
Tsung. The sorcerer disables one of Liu Kang's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:34.000 --> 00:04:38.560
arms with a curse, but the Shaolin warrior&nbsp;
manages to defeat Shang Tsung regardless.

00:04:39.520 --> 00:04:44.400
Despite being manipulated by his grandmaster&nbsp;
and losing Smoke to the cyborg program,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:44.400 --> 00:04:47.120
Kuai Liang still harbors deep-seated anger toward&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:47.120 --> 00:04:50.560
Scorpion for the murder of his&nbsp;
brother Bi-Han. Interestingly,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:50.560 --> 00:04:54.560
Scorpion regrets killing Bi-Han, and has&nbsp;
learned that vengeance is an empty pursuit.

00:04:55.120 --> 00:04:59.760
Despite their differences, the duo determines&nbsp;
that they must join forces against the Lin Kuei&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:59.760 --> 00:05:04.240
cyborgs to stop them from using the key to&nbsp;
unleashing disaster upon all the realms.

00:05:04.240 --> 00:05:08.320
Their attempt to stop the impending doom is&nbsp;
foiled, however, when the two are overwhelmed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:08.320 --> 00:05:12.560
by the cyborgs. Scorpion is taken to the&nbsp;
Temple of Elements and forced to place&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:12.560 --> 00:05:17.520
his hands upon the door to open the ancient&nbsp;
vault. Inside the temple lies a Kamidogu,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:17.520 --> 00:05:22.320
one piece of many that when collected summon the&nbsp;
power of the One Being. The Lin Kuei grandmaster&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:22.320 --> 00:05:26.880
delivers this piece of the Kamidogu to Shinnok,&nbsp;
who is revealed to be the clan's client.

00:05:27.760 --> 00:05:32.000
In the lore of the "Mortal Kombat" video&nbsp;
games, particularly "Mortal Kombat: Deception,"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:32.000 --> 00:05:36.320
the One Being is considered the progenitor&nbsp;
of the realms in the Mortal Kombat storyline.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:36.320 --> 00:05:40.960
Before life as we know it among the realms truly&nbsp;
began, the One Being and the elder gods existed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:40.960 --> 00:05:45.360
as the deities within the universe. The elder&nbsp;
gods sought to remove the One Being's limitless&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:45.360 --> 00:05:51.040
power by dividing the deity among the realms as&nbsp;
artifacts known as Kamidogu. Anyone capable of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:51.040 --> 00:05:56.480
uniting the Kamidogu pieces with a sacred amulet&nbsp;
would obtain the godlike power of the One Being.

00:05:56.480 --> 00:06:00.960
As the story goes in "Battle of the Realms," it&nbsp;
is known that the mad god Shinnok has vigorously&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:00.960 --> 00:06:05.280
sought the One Being's power so he can merge&nbsp;
the realms and wipe them out of existence.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:05.280 --> 00:06:10.480
The Lin Kuei grandmaster and his cyborg puppets&nbsp;
merely act as mindless mercenaries doing Shinnok's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:10.480 --> 00:06:15.520
bidding. Upon realizing Shinnok's true identity&nbsp;
after giving him the final Kamidogu piece,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:15.520 --> 00:06:19.600
it's apparent that the grandmaster knows he's&nbsp;
made a terrible mistake. But he doesn't get&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:19.600 --> 00:06:23.440
to sit with that reality long, as Shinnok&nbsp;
calls upon the forces of the Netherrealm&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:23.440 --> 00:06:28.720
to destroy the grandmaster and his cyborgs.&nbsp;
By the time Kuai Liang and Scorpion arrive,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:28.720 --> 00:06:32.560
it's too late: Shinnok has started&nbsp;
merging with the power of the One Being.

00:06:33.280 --> 00:06:37.280
After a long and arduous tournament with&nbsp;
plenty of death to go around, the tournament&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:37.280 --> 00:06:42.240
delivers one final blow: Raiden accepts the&nbsp;
challenge to face Shao Kahn in Mortal Kombat.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:42.240 --> 00:06:47.520
The barbaric dictator beats the former thunder&nbsp;
god and kills him, much to Liu Kang's horror.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:47.520 --> 00:06:51.440
But before Liu Kang's friend and mentor&nbsp;
meets his end, he is sure to tell Liu that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:51.440 --> 00:06:56.000
even though his parents died when he was very&nbsp;
young, they died protecting and loving him.

00:06:56.000 --> 00:07:00.480
This is the fire Liu Kang needs heading into his&nbsp;
fight with the Outworld leader. After finding&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:00.480 --> 00:07:05.360
some inner strength and harnessing his chi, Liu&nbsp;
Kang is able to dispel Shang Tsung's curse on his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:05.360 --> 00:07:10.480
arm and defeat Shao Kahn. He then frees Kitana&nbsp;
from her imprisonment, and the group begins to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:10.480 --> 00:07:14.720
celebrate the victory. But, unfortunately,&nbsp;
they're unable to get too far along in the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:14.720 --> 00:07:19.600
celebration before the elder gods appear and&nbsp;
alert Liu Kang to the impending challenge ahead.

00:07:20.240 --> 00:07:24.080
Shinnok takes on the power of the One&nbsp;
Being and grows to a massive size.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:24.080 --> 00:07:27.520
With the absorption of the deity's&nbsp;
power comes the merging of the realms.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:27.520 --> 00:07:32.000
All the realms begin blending together, which&nbsp;
means humans in Earthrealm are now at the mercy&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:32.000 --> 00:07:36.400
of the ravenous denizens of Outworld. While&nbsp;
the realms are consumed in chaos, the elder&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:36.400 --> 00:07:41.200
gods lend their power to Liu Kang so he can&nbsp;
attempt to defeat a seemingly invincible being.

00:07:41.200 --> 00:07:46.160
With his newfound power, Liu Kang takes the form&nbsp;
of a massive dragon not unlike the one you see in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:46.160 --> 00:07:50.960
the famous Mortal Kombat logo. Through the history&nbsp;
of the video game series, Liu Kang has been known&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:50.960 --> 00:07:56.400
to perform fatalities and animalities where he can&nbsp;
morph into a dragon and chomp on his opposition,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:56.400 --> 00:08:00.320
so we're in familiar territory with this&nbsp;
one. While Shinnok and Liu Kang engage in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:00.320 --> 00:08:04.560
a giant battle at the center of the merging&nbsp;
realms, the rest of Earth's champions scatter&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:04.560 --> 00:08:09.520
to assist helpless civilians from the chaos of&nbsp;
the moment. Liu Kang almost meets his match,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:09.520 --> 00:08:14.480
but the deadly duo consisting of the newly&nbsp;
adorned Sub-Zero and Scorpion intervene before&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:14.480 --> 00:08:18.960
the giant Shinnok-One-Being monstrosity&nbsp;
can deliver a killing blow to dragon Liu&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:18.960 --> 00:08:24.000
Kang. The dragon then manages to retaliate and&nbsp;
finishes off the giant deity for good. Then,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:24.000 --> 00:08:28.320
using his divine power, Liu Kang separates&nbsp;
the realms and puts things back in order.

00:08:29.120 --> 00:08:33.040
Nothing has been confirmed regarding a&nbsp;
"Mortal Kombat: Battle of the Realms" sequel,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:33.040 --> 00:08:37.520
but it's a strong possibility. After&nbsp;
all, why create a new MK series brand&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:37.520 --> 00:08:41.360
called "Mortal Kombat Legends"&nbsp;
and stop at only two titles? Also,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:41.360 --> 00:08:46.080
a few threads are left open for potential&nbsp;
future storylines. Shao Kahn has been defeated,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:46.080 --> 00:08:50.640
but he wasn't killed. In fact, Jax poses&nbsp;
a question in the film's final moments.

00:08:50.640 --> 00:08:55.440
On a happier note, the elder gods likely restored&nbsp;
Raiden to both life and his full thunder god&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:55.440 --> 00:09:00.560
glory. As the camera pans out of the arena into&nbsp;
the end credits, we can see the familiar lightning&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:00.560 --> 00:09:05.040
strike that often heralds Raiden's arrival. We&nbsp;
simply have to see Liu Kang and Lord Raiden's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:05.040 --> 00:09:10.080
reunion. Raiden's death was tragic for the young&nbsp;
warrior and it'd be nice to see the two tackle&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:10.080 --> 00:09:14.640
a new world-threatening issue together. "Mortal&nbsp;
Kombat" lore is filled to the brim with heroes and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:14.640 --> 00:09:19.520
villains, so there's no shortage of possibilities&nbsp;
for the future of this animated series.

